        "description": "Final approach targeting."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 334,
        "type": "arrival",
        "label": "Mars orbit insertion",
        "description": "Planned 2027. Captures into Mars orbit, then spirals down to a Phobos quasi-satellite orbit — a stable Mars-relative position that lets MMX hover near Phobos without orbiting it directly (Phobos's gravity is too small for a stable orbit)."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 334.01,
        "type": "edl_or_oi",
        "label": "Phobos sample collection",
        "description": "Planned 2028–2029. MMX will descend to Phobos's surface, collect ≥10g of regolith via a coring sampler, and ascend back. The samples return to Earth in 2031 — the first material returned from Mars's moons, expected to settle whether Phobos formed from captured asteroids or from an Earth-Moon-style giant impact on Mars."
      }
